{title: Smile}
{artist: Daniel Sullivan}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 124}

Verse 1
Everything that, I will ever do
I will strive that it would honor you
Everything that, I will ever say
I will strive that it would praise your name
Praise your name

So my countenance will not fall
And your glory will be seen by all

Verse 2
One of many of your sons am I
So I pray my life will testify
I have nothing, you are all I am
So I will let my light shine before men

These are things you’ve said to do 
That my words and thoughts might please you

Chorus
I will turn the other cheek 
I will walk the extra mile
I will always call out your name
Just so I can see you smile
And when I am on my knees
I will stand up in the trail
I will lose my life to find you
Just so I can see you smile

Verse 3
If I forsake, the lusts of my youth
I can call on you with a heart of truth
I’ll be a vessel, fit for my Masters hands
I will guard my heart with your commands

Chorus
I will turn the other cheek 
I will walk the extra mile
I will always call out your name
Just so I can see you smile
And when I am on my knees
I will stand up in the trail
I will lose my life to find you
Just so I can see you smile

